	When playing Nethack, I usually develop my main weapon(s) (the one(s) I 
start with) to Expert -- for roleplaying reasons: I think a character 
should be proficient with his/her main weapon. Some people will 
(rightly) say that your initial weapon is worthless and sometimes it's 
counter-productive in the long run as you might be developing a "wrong" 
weapon class that has no good advanced weapons. Granted I'm not 
experienced (the deepest I've been is level 18 in one lucky game), I 
don't have a good idea of advanced weapons. So here's my question: do 
you develop your starting weapon classes and why? Or do you dump them 
for a better weapon the first chance you get? Examples that come to mind 
is Healer's scalpel or archeologists bull whip... What do you think? You 
can also talk about other weapons/classes/examples without spoiling me 
too much. :)

